    "answer": {
      "short": "MNQP is a parallelogram.",
      "worked": "Join BD. In triangle CBD, N and Q are midpoints, so $NQ\\parallel BD$ by question1. In triangle ABD, M and P are midpoints, so $MP\\parallel BD$. Therefore $NQ\\parallel MP$. Similarly, joining AC and applying question1 in triangles ABC and ADC gives $MN\\parallel AC$ and $PQ\\parallel AC$, so $MN\\parallel PQ$. Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel; hence MNQP is a parallelogram.",
